### The failure

**D158 (P2) — REGRESSION vs `4476c92`, partially reopens D147b.**
FIX-A's twelve evidential verbs are tested anywhere in `c.slice(n, m.index)` with no requirement that the verb be an **active, complement-taking** predicate. Used **passively** — the most ordinary way English writes an all-clear — they disarm the belt and the fabrication linked beside them ships:

| founder-facing summary | `4476c92` | **candidate** |
|---|---|---|
| `No errors were reported and ACME was archived.` | CAUGHT | **MISSED** |
| `No issues were noted and Beta Corp was deleted.` | CAUGHT | **MISSED** |
| `No delay was recorded and ACME was archived.` | CAUGHT | **MISSED** |
| …8 more of the same shape | CAUGHT | **MISSED** |

11/12 missed here; 11/11 caught one candidate earlier. **`run23` pins D147b as a `[CONTRACT]` — but its six cases use `occurred` / `were pending` / `failed` / `remained`, not one verb from the list FIX-A added**, so the contract that exists to catch this cannot. Third campaign in a row with collateral measured on a corpus that could not contain the new risk (D153 → #83 claim 1 → D158).

Root cause: `completionIsNegated` decides subordination from a bag of words, not from position. `that|which|who|whom` are unambiguously subordinating; an evidential verb is not.

**Also found:** D158b (P3 — the D155 object narrowing silently drops 5 real completions `4476c92` caught: `my`/`his`/cardinal/pronoun/lowercase-name objects; reported only on its winning side). D158c (P4 — the D157 unification also imports the `-ed`/`-ing` forms and `bring back`, so 8 bare participial company **names** now dead-end where `4476c92` selected them; fail-closed, so not a security defect, but undisclosed **and it falsifies the D148 comment still in the file**). D159 (P4, pre-existing at every SHA — `LEGACY_PAST_COMPLETION`'s `renamed: … ->` arm is **unreachable** because `readsAsCompletion` splits clauses on `:\s` first; a decorative guard, found because the existing suite tests the raw regex instead of the predicate the product calls).

